			<dc:creator>Diego HH</dc:creator>
			<title>Postal codes and tessellations</title>
			<description>From postal points to areas using Voronoi polygons</description>
			<content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;I recently published my project &lt;a href=&quot;https://dieghernan.github.io/codigospostales/&quot;&gt;Postal codes of
Spain&lt;/a&gt;, with estimated postal
areas, an interactive map and GeoPackage downloads. But there is something we
have not looked at yet: how do those address points become polygons? The answer
is… &lt;strong&gt;Voronoi polygons&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded>
